---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro'
import { hospital } from '../data/site'
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  subtitle="The terms that govern your use of our website and online services."
  updated="September 2026"
>
  <h2>1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
  <p>
    By accessing or using this website ({hospital.domains.primary} and {hospital.domains.secondary}), you agree to be
    bound by these Terms of Service. If you do not agree with any part of these terms, please do not use this website.
  </p>

  <h2>2. About Our Services</h2>
  <p>
    This website provides general information about {hospital.name}, its departments, doctors, services, health camps,
    and a facility to request OPD appointments, teleconsultations and camp registrations. You receive an instant email
    acknowledgement of your request, and our team may contact you using the details you provide if any clarification or
    change is required.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Appointment Bookings</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Please provide accurate contact and health details so we can process your request correctly.</li>
    <li>We may need to reschedule or cancel appointments due to unforeseen circumstances; we will inform you as early as possible.</li>
    <li>Repeated no-shows may lead to future online bookings being confirmed by phone.</li>
    <li>For emergencies, do not rely on online booking — call {hospital.phones.emergency}, or dial 112 (all-in-one emergency) or 108 (free ambulance).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Cancellations, No-Shows and Refunds</h2>
  <p>
    Cancellation, no-show, refund and billing-correction terms are set out in our
    <a href="/refund-cancellation">Refund &amp; Cancellation Policy</a>, which forms part of these terms.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Payments and Billing</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Where online payment is offered, it is optional. You may instead pay at the hospital reception by cash, UPI or card.</li>
    <li>Online payments are processed by a third-party payment gateway. We do not store your full card or banking credentials on this website.</li>
    <li>An itemised bill is provided for services rendered. Verified billing errors are corrected in accordance with our refund policy.</li>
    <li>Treatment is never denied in a medical emergency on the ground of inability to pay, in accordance with applicable law.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. Teleconsultation</h2>
  <p>
    Teleconsultations are governed by our <a href="/telemedicine">Telemedicine &amp; Teleconsultation</a> terms and consent
    notice, prepared in line with the Telemedicine Practice Guidelines, 2020. Please read them before your consultation.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Medical Disclaimer</h2>
  <p>
    Content on this website is for general information only and is not a substitute for professional medical advice,
    diagnosis, or treatment. Always seek the advice of a qualified health provider with any questions you may have
    regarding a medical condition. Never disregard professional medical advice because of something you read on this site.
    See our full <a href="/disclaimer">Medical Disclaimer</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    Our handling of your personal data is described in our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>, prepared under the DPDP
    Act, 2023, which forms part of these terms.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Acceptable Use</h2>
  <p>You agree not to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Use this website for any unlawful purpose or to misrepresent your identity.</li>
    <li>Attempt to gain unauthorised access to the website, its servers, or connected systems.</li>
    <li>Interfere with the normal operation of the website or attempt to overload it.</li>
    <li>Submit false information through forms on this site.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>10. Intellectual Property</h2>
  <p>
    All content on this website — including text, graphics, logos, and design — is the property of {hospital.name}
    or its licensors and is protected by applicable intellectual property laws. You may not reproduce, distribute,
    or use our content without prior written permission, except for personal, non-commercial use.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Limitation of Liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the maximum extent permitted by law, {hospital.name} shall not be liable for any direct, indirect, incidental,
    or consequential damages arising from your use of, or inability to use, this website. The website is provided
    "as is" without warranties of any kind, express or implied.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Third-Party Links</h2>
  <p>
    Links to external websites are provided for convenience. We do not endorse and are not responsible for the content
    or practices of third-party sites.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Changes to These Terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may revise these terms at any time. Changes take effect when posted on this page. Your continued use of the
    website constitutes acceptance of the updated terms.
  </p>

  <h2>14. Governing Law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of India and the state of Haryana. Any disputes shall be subject to the
    jurisdiction of the courts in Jind, Haryana.
  </p>

  <h2>15. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    For questions about these terms, contact us at {hospital.email} or call {hospital.phones.reception}.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
